# F3 - MEDICATION CHART

## Product Requirements Document (PRD)

***

## 1\. Overview

**App Name:** F3 - Medication Chart

F3 - Medication Chart is a Progressive Web App (PWA) designed to serve as a comprehensive digital medication management system for individuals, caregivers, and healthcare support staff. The application enables users to record, manage, and track all medication details — including dosage, frequency, start and end dates, renewal schedules, and file attachments such as prescriptions and lab reports. Users receive timely notifications (1, 2, or 3 days before renewal) with date and time precision, ensuring no medication lapse or missed renewal. All records are fully editable, color-coded for quick visual identification of renewal urgency, and printable with renewal date/time filtering for reports or handoffs.

**Target Audience:** Patients managing chronic conditions, family caregivers, home healthcare workers, nursing staff, and clinics managing multiple patient medication schedules. The core problem the app solves is the fragmented, paper-based, or error-prone nature of medication tracking — especially around renewal deadlines — by centralizing all medication data, reminders, and documentation in a single accessible PWA.

***

## 2\. Essential Core Features

### 2.1 Medication Management (CRUD)

* **Add Medication:** Full form to enter medication name, dosage, form (tablet/capsule/liquid/injection/other), frequency (e.g., once daily, twice daily, every X hours, custom), prescribing doctor, pharmacy, notes, start date/time, end date/time, and renewal date/time.
* **Edit Medication:** All fields in the medication record are fully editable at any time, including all dates, times, frequency, and attachments.
* **Delete Medication:** Soft delete with confirmation prompt to avoid accidental removal.
* **View Medication Detail:** Full detail screen showing all stored information for a single medication.

### 2.2 Frequency Management

* Predefined frequency options: Once daily, Twice daily, Three times daily, Four times daily, Every X hours (custom), Weekly, As needed (PRN), Custom schedule.
* Custom frequency builder allowing users to define specific days and times.
* Frequency displayed prominently on medication cards.

### 2.3 File Attachment Management

* Upload and attach multiple files per medication (prescriptions, doctor notes, insurance documents, lab reports).
* Supported file types: PDF, JPG, PNG, DOCX.
* Preview attached files within the app.
* Delete or replace attachments at any time.
* Attachments stored securely via Supabase Storage.

### 2.4 Renewal Scheduling & Notifications

* Set renewal date and time per medication.
* Configure renewal reminder lead time: 1 day before, 2 days before, and/or 3 days before (multiple selections allowed).
* Push notifications (via PWA Web Push API) sent at configured lead times on the set time.
* In-app notification center to view pending and past renewal alerts.
* Notification status (sent/pending/dismissed) tracked per medication.

### 2.5 Color-Coded Renewal Identification

* Each medication card and list item is visually color-coded based on renewal urgency:
    * 🔴 **Red:** Renewal due today or overdue.
    * 🟠 **Orange:** Renewal due within 1 day.
    * 🟡 **Yellow:** Renewal due within 2–3 days.
    * 🟢 **Green:** Renewal not due soon (more than 3 days away).
    * ⚫ **Grey:** No renewal date set or medication ended.
* Color legend visible on the dashboard for reference.

### 2.6 Print & Export

* Print medication chart filtered by renewal date/time range.
* Print view shows: medication name, dosage, frequency, start/end dates, renewal date, doctor, pharmacy, and notes.
* Option to export as PDF (browser print-to-PDF or generated PDF via client-side library).
* Print filter: select date range for renewal dates to include in the report.
* Clean, formatted print layout with F3 Medication Chart branding and patient/user name.

### 2.7 Dashboard & Filtering

* Dashboard overview showing all medications grouped or sorted by renewal urgency (color-coded).
* Filter medications by: renewal date range, color/urgency status, active/inactive/all status, frequency type.
* Search bar to find medications by name or doctor.
* Sort by: renewal date (ascending/descending), medication name (A–Z), start date.

### 2.8 User Authentication

* Secure sign-up and login via Supabase Auth (email/password).
* Password reset via email.
* Optional: User profile setup with name (used in print headers).

### 2.9 User Profile & Settings

* Edit profile name and contact details.
* Manage notification preferences (enable/disable push notifications, select global reminder lead times).
* View app version and account details.
* Log out.

