## 4\. Design Preferences

### Interface

The app features a clean, clinical-yet-approachable mobile-first interface with card-based layouts, strong color-coded renewal indicators, and intuitive bottom navigation — delivering a feel similar to a polished health management app with clear visual hierarchy and accessibility-first design.

### Color Palette

| Role | Color | Hex |
| ---- | ----- | --- |
| Primary | Deep Medical Blue | `#1A5276` |
| Secondary | Soft White / Light Grey | `#F4F6F9` |
| Accent | Teal / Cyan | `#17A589` |
| Danger / Overdue | Red | `#E74C3C` |
| Warning 1-day | Orange | `#E67E22` |
| Warning 2-3 days | Amber Yellow | `#F1C40F` |
| Safe / On-track | Soft Green | `#27AE60` |
| No Renewal / Inactive | Medium Grey | `#95A5A6` |
| Text Primary | Dark Charcoal | `#1C2833` |
| Text Secondary | Medium Grey | `#717D7E` |

### Typography

* **Headings:** `Inter` (Bold, 700) — clean, modern, highly legible on mobile
* **Body/Labels:** `Inter` (Regular/Medium, 400/500)
* **Medication Names (Cards):** `Inter` Semi-Bold (600) for emphasis
* **Monospace (dates/times):** `JetBrains Mono` or `Roboto Mono` for consistent date/time display

### Additional Design Considerations

* Bottom navigation bar with 4–5 tabs as primary navigation pattern for mobile PWA.
* Floating Action Button (FAB) for adding new medications on dashboard and list screens.
* Card-based medication items with a left-side colored vertical stripe indicating renewal urgency color.
* Pull-to-refresh on the medication list.
* Full-screen modal sheets for Add/Edit medication forms (slides up from bottom).
* Haptic feedback simulation via CSS micro-animations on button interactions.
* Dark mode support (optional phase 2 consideration; foundation to be laid with Tailwind dark classes).
* All interactive elements have minimum 44×44px touch targets per mobile accessibility guidelines.

