## 7\. User Flow

### Flow 1: New User Onboarding & First Medication

1. User opens the PWA in browser or from installed home screen icon.
2. Splash screen loads (2 seconds) → detects no session → redirects to `/login`.
3. User taps "Don't have an account? Sign Up" → navigates to `/signup`.
4. User enters Full Name, Email, Password, Confirm Password → taps "Create Account".
5. Supabase creates account → user auto-logged in → redirected to `/dashboard`.
6. Dashboard shows empty state: "No medications yet. Tap + to add your first medication."
7. User taps the central "+" FAB in bottom navigation.
8. Add Medication modal slides up from bottom.
9. User fills in: Medication Name ("Metformin"), Form (Tablet), Dosage (500mg), Frequency (Twice Daily).
10. User selects Start Date (today) and sets Renewal Date (30 days from today) and Renewal Time (09:00 AM).
11. User selects renewal reminder chips: "1 Day Before" and "2 Days Before".
12. User taps "+ Attach Files" → device file picker opens → selects prescription PDF.
13. PDF attachment appears in the form as a chip.
14. User adds Doctor name and Pharmacy name.
15. User taps "Save Medication."
16. Modal dismisses → Dashboard now shows the new medication card with a **Green** color stripe (renewal 30 days away).
17. Success toast appears: "Metformin added successfully."
18. Browser prompts for push notification permission (triggered on first notification-enabled medication save).
19. User taps "Allow" → notification subscription stored in Supabase.

***

### Flow 2: Viewing & Editing a Medication

1. From `/dashboard`, user sees medication cards sorted by renewal urgency.
2. User notices a card with an **Orange** stripe ("Renewal in 1 Day").
3. User taps the card → navigates to `/medication/:id`.
4. Detail screen shows all medication info with orange header banner.
5. User sees the renewal date/time, notification settings, and existing attachments.
6. User taps the Edit (pencil) icon in the top app bar.
7. Edit Medication modal slides up with all fields pre-populated.
8. User updates the Renewal Date to 7 days from now and adjusts dosage.
9. User taps "Update."
10. Modal dismisses → detail screen refreshes → color stripe changes to **Green** (now 7 days away).
11. Toast: "Medication updated successfully."

***

### Flow 3: Managing Attachments

1. User is on `/medication/:id` detail screen.
2. User scrolls to "Attachments" section → sees 1 existing prescription PDF.
3. User taps the PDF thumbnail → full-screen preview/viewer opens.
4. User closes preview → back on detail screen.
5. User taps "+ Add Attachment" → file picker opens → selects a JPG image (lab report).
6. New image thumbnail appears in attachments grid.
7. User long-presses (or taps × icon) on the old PDF attachment → confirmation dialog: "Remove this attachment?"
8. User confirms → attachment deleted from Supabase Storage and removed from view.

***

### Flow 4: Receiving & Acting on Renewal Notification

1. It is 1 day before a medication's renewal date at 09:00 AM.
2. Supabase Edge Function triggers Web Push notification to user's device.
3. User receives push notification: "💊 Metformin renewal due tomorrow! Tap to view details."
4. User taps notification → PWA opens (or foregrounds) → navigates directly to `/medication/:id`.
5. Color stripe is now **Orange** (1 day away).
6. User arranges refill and returns to edit screen to update the renewal date.
7. Notification is logged as "Sent" in Supabase notification\_logs table.
8. In-app `/notifications` screen shows the notification under "Sent" tab.

***

### Flow 5: Printing a Filtered Medication Chart

1. From `/dashboard`, user taps the print/share icon (available in top app bar or via FAB menu).
2. Print / Export modal slides up.
3. User sets Renewal Date Range: From "this week" To "next 30 days."
4. User selects color filters: "Overdue" + "Due in 1–3 Days."
5. Print preview updates to show 3 matching medications.
6. User taps "Print / Save as PDF."
7. Browser native print dialog opens.
8. User selects "Save as PDF" or sends to printer.
9. Printed report shows: App name header, date printed, user name, and a clean table of matching medications with all details.
10. User closes print dialog → modal dismisses.

***

### Flow 6: Notification Preferences & Settings

1. User taps "Settings" tab in bottom navigation → `/settings`.
2. User sees Push Notifications toggle is ON.
3. User scrolls to "Default Reminder" chips → currently "1 Day Before" is selected.
4. User taps "3 Days Before" to also enable it.
5. User scrolls to Profile section → taps "Edit Profile" → updates their name.
6. User taps "Save" → profile name updated → used in future print report headers.
7. User taps "Log Out" → confirmation prompt appears.
8. User confirms → session cleared → redirected to `/login`.

